Ignoring the race condition (we could receive our farewell before we’re greeted!), we
can see that we have two branches of our program running concurrently. We’ve set up
the standard preemption method by creating a done channel and passing it down
through our call-graph. If we close the done channel at any point in main, both
branches will be canceled.
